{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 29,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Job again took up his parable, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that I were as in the months of old,\nAs in the days when God watched over me;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When his lamp shined upon my head,\nAnd by his light I walked through darkness;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As I was in the ripeness of my days,\nWhen the friendship of God was upon my tent;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the Almighty was yet with me,\nAnd my children were about me;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When my steps were washed with butter,\nAnd the rock poured me out streams of oil!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I went forth to the gate unto the city,\nWhen I prepared my seat in the street,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The young men saw me and hid themselves,\nAnd the aged rose up and stood;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The princes refrained from talking,\nAnd laid their hand on their mouth;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The voice of the nobles was hushed,\nAnd their tongue cleaved to the roof of their mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For when the ear heard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", then it blessed me;\nAnd when the eye saw ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", it gave witness unto me:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because I delivered the poor that cried,\nThe fatherless also, that had none to help him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The blessing of him that was ready to perish came upon me;\nAnd I caused the widow’s heart to sing for joy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I put on righteousness, and it clothed me:\nMy justice was as a robe and a diadem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I was eyes to the blind,\nAnd feet was I to the lame.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I was a father to the needy:\nAnd the cause of him that I knew not I searched out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I brake the jaws of the unrighteous,\nAnd plucked the prey out of his teeth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then I said, I shall die in my nest,\nAnd I shall multiply my days as the sand:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My root is spread out to the waters,\nAnd the dew lieth all night upon my branch:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My glory is fresh in me,\nAnd my bow is renewed in my hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Unto me men gave ear, and waited,\nAnd kept silence for my counsel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "After my words they spake not again;\nAnd my speech distilled upon them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they waited for me as for the rain;\nAnd they opened their mouth wide ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the latter rain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I smiled on them, when they had no confidence;\nAnd the light of my countenance they cast not down.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.29.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.29.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I chose out their way, and sat ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " chief,\nAnd dwelt as a king in the army,\nAs one that comforteth the mourners.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
